{"seq":44,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24762"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-004, category 2; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Medical Sciences] Diabetes develops as the result of a problem with which specific organ in the body?\nA. Pancreas B. Liver C. Kidney\nAnswer: A. The pancreas is responsible for producing insulin, a hormone that regulates blood sugar. In diabetes, either the pancreas does not produce enough insulin (Type 1) or the body becomes resistant to insulin’s effects (Type 2).\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-004.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"Which organ produces insulin, the hormone whose lack or ineffectiveness causes diabetes?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welches Organ produziert Insulin, das Hormon, dessen Mangel oder Unwirksamkeit Diabetes verursacht?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-004","category":2}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Medical Sciences] Diabetes develops as the result of a problem with which specific organ in the body?\nA. Pancreas B. Liver C. Kidney\nAnswer: A. The pancreas is responsible for producing insulin, a hormone that regulates blood sugar. In diabetes, either the pancreas does not produce enough insulin (Type 1) or the body becomes resistant to insulin’s effects (Type 2)."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f00762"}],"hash":"d9925daaab07"},
